---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const schema = `[{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": ["LocalBusiness", "RoofingContractor"],
    "name": "Happy Roof LLC",
    "url": "https://happyroof.com",
    "telephone": "+1-813-595-7663",
    "email": "info@happyroof.com",
    "description": "Free professional roof inspections in Tampa Bay. Licensed, insured roofing contractor. FL License #CCC1337380.",
    "image": "/Brand%20Assets/Happy%20Roof%20Logo.jpeg",
    "logo": "/Brand%20Assets/Happy%20Roof%20Logo.jpeg",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "streetAddress": "141 Stevens Ave #12","addressLocality": "Oldsmar",
      "addressRegion": "FL","postalCode": "34677","addressCountry": "US"
    },
    "hasCredential": "Florida Roofing Contractor License #CCC1337380",
    "dateModified": "2026-04-25"
  },{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What sets Happy Roof apart?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "We're a licensed Florida roofing contractor (FL #CCC1337380) with full liability and workers' comp insurance, and every inspection is done by a licensed inspector. We take the same approach to inspections as we do to repairs and replacements, so if your roof looks like it's already in good shape, we'll tell you that. If it needs attention, we'll always explain exactly what and why. You get a written report with photos either way, and no one is going to pressure you into a decision on the spot." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is the roof inspection really free?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, completely. We offer free inspections because it's the proper way to start a conversation with a homeowner, and because most people who get an honest look at their roof end up working with us anyway. We'd rather earn your business by being useful upfront than by making you feel pressured." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How long does a roof inspection take?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Most residential inspections take 30 to 60 minutes depending on the size and pitch of the roof. Commercial properties or larger multi-story homes tend to take just a little bit longer than that. Either way, you'll have the written report in your inbox within 24 hours." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What does a roof inspection include?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Our inspection covers shingles or roofing material condition, flashing and sealant integrity, gutter and drainage systems, soffit and fascia, attic ventilation, signs of leaks or moisture damage, and structural integrity. You receive a detailed written report with photos." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How often should I get my roof inspected in Florida?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Once a year at a minimum, or after any major storm, since Florida's heat and UV exposure put more stress on roofing materials than most climates. If your roof is 15 years or older, you might want to consider having it inspected twice a year." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do I need to be home for the inspection?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "It might be helpful, but it's not required. If you're there, our inspector can walk you through the findings right then and there and answer any questions you may have. That said, if you can't be home, we'll of course still conduct the inspection and send you the full report afterward." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Could a roof inspection help with my insurance claim?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Absolutely. If we find storm damage or other covered issues, we'll document everything with photos and written details that your adjuster can work from directly. We work with all major Florida insurance carriers and can meet with your adjuster on-site if that helps. On the other hand, if you're buying or selling a home, a professional inspection can give buyers confidence in what they're purchasing and give sellers a chance to address anything before it becomes a negotiating issue at closing. For insurance renewals, we can also provide wind mitigation and 4-point inspection documentation if your carrier requires it." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What's the best time of year for a roof inspection in Tampa Bay?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The single best time in Florida is SPRING, specifically March through May, before hurricane season starts June 1. Weather is mild, materials aren't heat-softened, and you have time to complete any repairs before the first tropical system arrives. Here's the full seasonal breakdown for Tampa Bay: SPRING (March-May) is the top-priority window, when you want the annual professional inspection done and any needed repairs scheduled. SUMMER (June-August) is inspection-only-after-storms: surface temps on shingles and TPO exceed 150F on afternoon roofs, foot traffic causes damage, and any repair sealants cure poorly in the heat. If a storm hits, get inspected within 5 days for insurance-claim timelines. FALL (September-November) is the post-hurricane assessment window: even without a direct hit, cumulative wind stress from a Florida hurricane season causes seam separations, lifted shingles, and hidden underlayment damage that only shows up under close inspection. WINTER (December-February) is repair-and-renewal season: the driest weather in Tampa Bay, ideal for larger repair or replacement work, and the window when most Florida homeowner insurance policies renew (a fresh inspection report is often required for wind-mitigation credits on renewal). Rule of thumb: schedule the annual inspection in spring, add a second inspection in fall if any tropical system passed within 200 miles, and never skip a post-storm inspection." }
      }
    ]
  },{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "serviceType": "Roof Inspection",
    "provider": { "@type": "RoofingContractor", "name": "Happy Roof LLC", "telephone": "+1-813-595-7663", "url": "https://happyroof.com" },
    "areaServed": { "@type": "State", "name": "Florida" },
    "description": "Free professional roof inspections in Tampa Bay. Comprehensive assessment of shingles, flashing, ventilation, structure, and drainage. Licensed contractor FL #CCC1337380."
  },{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Free Roof Inspection",
    "description": "Professional roof inspection with detailed written report including assessment of shingles, flashing, ventilation, structure, and drainage.",
    "provider": {"@type": "RoofingContractor", "name": "Happy Roof LLC"},
    "areaServed": {"@type": "City", "name": "Tampa Bay"},
    "offers": {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "priceRange": "$0",
      "priceCurrency": "USD"
    }
  }]`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Free Roof Inspection in Tampa Bay | Happy Roof"
  description="Looking for someone to check your roof for storm damage or leaks? We offer free roof inspections for home and business owners across Tampa Bay."
  canonical="https://happyroof.com/roof-inspection"
  ogDescription="Free professional roof inspections in Tampa Bay. Storm damage, leaks, wear, and more. We check it all. FL #CCC1337380."
  schema={schema}
>

<style is:inline>
.check-dot{width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(230,168,23,.1);flex-shrink:0;margin-top:.15rem}
    .step-num{width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(230,168,23,.1);font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.25rem;color:#E6A817;flex-shrink:0}
</style>

<!-- PAGE HERO -->
<section class="pt-32 pb-20 relative overflow-hidden" style="background:#F5F5F5;border-bottom:1px solid #E5E5E5">
  <div class="hero-photo-bg" style="background-image:url('/Brand%20Assets/Photos/roof-replacement-project-tampa-bay.jpg')"></div>
  <div class="hero-photo-overlay"></div>
  <div class="relative z-10 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 text-center">
    <p class="sl gp mb-4">Free Roof Inspections</p>
    <h1 class="font-display font-black tracking-tightest mb-5" style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-size:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem);line-height:.92;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#1A1A1A">
      FREE ROOF INSPECTION<br/><span class="gt">IN TAMPA BAY.</span>
    </h1>
    <p style="color:#1A1A1A;font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.75;font-weight:600;max-width:680px;margin:0 auto 1rem">
      A roof inspection is one of those things that's easy to put off until something goes wrong. At Happy Roof, we make it easy to stay ahead of problems with free inspections for homeowners and commercial property owners across Tampa Bay.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#1A1A1A;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.8;max-width:620px;margin:0 auto 1rem;border-left:3px solid #E6A817;padding-left:1.25rem">
      We've done thousands of them over 30 years in the industry, and whether your roof needs attention or is holding up just fine, we'll tell you exactly what we find. Call (813) 595-7663 to schedule.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-2xl mx-auto" style="color:#555555;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75">
      Your roof doesn't fail on the day it leaks. It failed months ago. By the time water comes through your ceiling, the underlayment is compromised, the decking may be rotting, and what was a $400 repair is now a $4,000 problem. A 30-minute inspection is the cheapest insurance policy you'll ever buy.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-2xl mx-auto mt-4" style="color:#777;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.75">
      Happy Roof provides free professional roof inspections throughout Tampa Bay, including Tampa, St. Petersburg, Clearwater, and surrounding cities. Our licensed team (FL #CCC1337380) inspects shingles, flashing, gutters, ventilation, and structural integrity, then delivers a detailed photo report within 24 hours. No charge, no obligation. Used for real estate transactions, insurance documentation, and preventive maintenance. Call (813) 595-7663 to schedule.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 justify-center mt-8">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-t">Schedule Free Inspection <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
      <a href="tel:8135957663" class="btn-o call-tracking-number">Call (813) 595-7663</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INFO STRIP -->
<div style="background:#FFFFFF;border-top:2px solid #E6A817;border-bottom:1px solid #E0E0E0;padding:.85rem 0">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-8 gap-y-2 font-display font-bold text-sm tracking-widest" style="color:#1A1A1A;text-transform:uppercase;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif">
      <span>Tampa Bay, FL</span>
      <span style="color:#E6A817">·</span>
      <span>CCC1337380</span>
      <span style="color:#E6A817">·</span>
      <span>HappyRoof.com</span>
      <span style="color:#E6A817">·</span>
      <span style="color:#3B9FD9">(813) 595-7663</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- WHY A ROOF INSPECTION MATTERS -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#FFFFFF">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-14 items-start">
      <div>
        <p class="sl gt mb-3">Why It Matters</p>
        <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1.5rem">WHY YOU SHOULD SCHEDULE AN INSPECTION</h2>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          Most roofs don't fail all at once. Problems usually start months or years beforehand as something small. A professional inspection is how you catch things like a patch of shingles that's been losing granules while it's still inexpensive to fix.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          In Florida especially, where heat and a six-month storm season put roofs under a lot more stress than most climates, staying ahead is almost always less expensive than reacting to it. For a complete season-by-season guide, see our <a href="/blog/roof-maintenance-checklist" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">roof maintenance checklist for Tampa Bay homeowners</a>.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          Roof condition also directly affects your homeowner's insurance. Many Florida insurance companies now require a roof inspection before issuing or renewing a policy. A documented inspection from a licensed contractor like Happy Roof can help you maintain coverage, secure better rates, and provide evidence for claims if storm damage occurs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="scard p-6">
          <div class="check"><div class="check-dot"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="3"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg></div><div><strong style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem">Catch Problems Early</strong><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.25rem">Small cracks, loose flashing, and worn sealant can be repaired for a fraction of what a full replacement costs. Early detection saves thousands.</p></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scard p-6">
          <div class="check"><div class="check-dot"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="3"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg></div><div><strong style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem">Protect Your Insurance</strong><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.25rem">Florida insurers increasingly require current roof inspections. A documented assessment helps maintain coverage and supports claims.</p></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scard p-6">
          <div class="check"><div class="check-dot"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="3"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg></div><div><strong style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem">Extend Your Roof's Lifespan</strong><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.25rem">Regular inspections paired with timely repairs can add 5-10 years to your roof's life, delaying the cost of a full replacement.</p></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scard p-6">
          <div class="check"><div class="check-dot"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="3"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg></div><div><strong style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem">Storm Preparedness</strong><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.25rem">Knowing your roof's condition before hurricane season gives you time to make repairs and strengthens your home's protection.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT WE INSPECT -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#F5F5F5;border-top:1px solid #E5E5E5;border-bottom:1px solid #E5E5E5">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
      <p class="sl gp mb-3">Inspection Checklist</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em">WHAT'S INCLUDED IN OUR FREE ROOF INSPECTIONS</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <div class="scard p-6">
        <div class="step-num mb-4">01</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">Roofing Material Condition</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.7">We'll examine every visible shingle, tile, or metal panel for signs of cracking, blistering, granule loss, displacement, or rust. Surface-level damage that looks minor from the ground could be letting in water at the seams.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scard p-6">
        <div class="step-num mb-4">02</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">Flashing and Sealant Integrity</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.7">Flashing is the metal that seals the joints where your roof meets a chimney, vent, skylight, or wall. It's also where the majority of leaks start. Our team will check every piece for rust, separation, loose edges, and sealant that's dried out and pulled away from the surface.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scard p-6">
        <div class="step-num mb-4">03</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">Gutters and Drainage</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.7">Clogged gutters and drainage that isn't working the way it should can cause water to back up along the roofline and start working its way into the fascia. We'll check how well your gutters are attached and whether the downspouts are moving water far enough away from the foundation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scard p-6">
        <div class="step-num mb-4">04</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">Soffit and Fascia</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.7">Soffit and fascia protect the edges of a roof and provide ventilation pathways to keep your attic from overheating. We keep an eye out for things like rot, pest damage, gaps that could let moisture or animals into the attic, and any deterioration that might be hiding behind peeling paint.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scard p-6">
        <div class="step-num mb-4">05</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">Attic and Ventilation</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.7">Poor attic ventilation is one of the most common causes of premature roof wear in Florida, and it's easy to miss from the outside. We'll check ridge vents, soffit vents, and insulation levels for adequate airflow, and look for any signs of moisture or mold while we're up there.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scard p-6">
        <div class="step-num mb-4">06</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">Structural Integrity</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.7">We'll check the roof deck, rafters, and trusses for sagging, water damage, and any compromised fasteners. Structural problems are usually subtle, but they can get serious pretty quickly once wind and rain are involved. If something looks off, we'll document it and explain what it means and what your options are.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- OUR INSPECTION PROCESS -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#FFFFFF">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
      <p class="sl gt mb-3">How It Works</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em">OUR PROCESS</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
      <div class="flex gap-5 items-start">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <div>
          <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.35rem">Schedule</h3>
          <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75">Give us a call at <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a> or fill out our contact form. Most inspections can be booked within a few business days, and we'll confirm a time that works for you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-5 items-start">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <div>
          <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.35rem">On-Site Inspection</h3>
          <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75">A licensed Happy Roof inspector will arrive and work through the full checklist above, exterior surfaces, flashing, gutters, soffit, fascia, and attic space. We'll photograph everything we find.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-5 items-start">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <div>
          <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.35rem">Written Report</h3>
          <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75">You'll receive a detailed report with photos documenting your roof's condition and any areas of concern within 24 hours. If repairs or replacement are needed, we'll include an itemized estimate. Or, we'll let you know if everything looks good as-is, too.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SEASONAL BREAKDOWN | Best time of year -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#FFFFFF;border-top:1px solid #E5E5E5">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <p class="sl gt mb-3">Best Time of Year</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1rem">WHAT IS THE BEST TIME OF YEAR FOR A ROOF INSPECTION IN TAMPA BAY?</h2>
      <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto">March through May is usually the best window since the weather tends to be cooperative and anything we find can be repaired before hurricane season begins on June 1. That said, every season plays a different role in Florida's roof-care calendar. Here's when to schedule, and what each window is actually good for.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-8">
      <!-- SPRING -->
      <div style="background:#FFFFFF;border:2px solid rgba(230,168,23,.35);border-radius:14px;padding:1.5rem;position:relative">
        <div style="position:absolute;top:-10px;left:1.25rem;background:#E6A817;color:#FFFFFF;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.1em;padding:.2rem .6rem;border-radius:100px;text-transform:uppercase">Top Priority</div>
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.05rem;color:#E6A817;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:.75rem 0 .35rem">Spring &middot; Mar-May</p>
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.15rem;color:#1A1A1A;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 .55rem">Annual inspection window</p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">The single best window in Florida. Mild weather, materials aren't heat-softened, and you have time to complete any repairs <strong>before hurricane season starts June 1</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- SUMMER -->
      <div style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E0E0E0;border-radius:14px;padding:1.5rem">
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.05rem;color:#3B9FD9;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 .35rem">Summer &middot; Jun-Aug</p>
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.15rem;color:#1A1A1A;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 .55rem">Only after storms</p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Roof surface temps exceed 150&deg;F on afternoons; foot traffic causes damage and sealants cure poorly. If a tropical system hits, get inspected <strong>within 5 days</strong> for insurance-claim timelines.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- FALL -->
      <div style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E0E0E0;border-radius:14px;padding:1.5rem">
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.05rem;color:#E6A817;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 .35rem">Fall &middot; Sep-Nov</p>
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.15rem;color:#1A1A1A;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 .55rem">Post-hurricane assessment</p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Even without a direct hit, cumulative wind stress causes seam separations, lifted shingles, and hidden underlayment damage. Book <strong>if any tropical system passed within 200 miles</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- WINTER -->
      <div style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E0E0E0;border-radius:14px;padding:1.5rem">
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.05rem;color:#3B9FD9;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 .35rem">Winter &middot; Dec-Feb</p>
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.15rem;color:#1A1A1A;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 .55rem">Repair &amp; insurance renewal</p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Tampa Bay's driest weather, ideal for larger repair or replacement work. Most FL homeowner policies renew in this window and often require a fresh inspection for <strong>wind-mitigation credits</strong>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:center;background:#F7F7F7;border:1px solid #E0E0E0;border-radius:12px;padding:1.25rem 2rem">
      <p style="color:#1A1A1A;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0"><strong>Rule of thumb for Tampa Bay:</strong> schedule the annual inspection in spring, add a second in fall if any tropical system passed nearby, and never skip a post-storm inspection.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHEN TO GET AN INSPECTION -->
