        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">Once a year at a minimum, or after any major storm, since Florida's heat and UV exposure put more stress on roofing materials than most climates. If your roof is 15 years or older, you might want to consider having it inspected twice a year. For a full season-by-season maintenance guide, check out our <a href="/roof-maintenance" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">roof maintenance for Tampa Bay homeowners</a>.</div>
